%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 6653ef5d86c7abb41b8c7cb3f6f286e0, type: 3}
  m_Name: CompareLesson
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Lesson
  title: Waterfall VS  Agile
  linkedModule: Computer_Graphics
  codeLines:
  - Waterfall plan
  - Agile plan
  - Time passes
  - Change request
  - Result
  steps:
  - highlightLine: -1
    action: none
    value: 0
    param: 
    explanation: Two teams build the same product. The WATERFALL lane and the AGILE
      lane share one time axis in weeks. Walk around the timeline and compare them
    narration: {fileID: 0}
  - highlightLine: 0
    action: add
    value: 0
    param: S|A|Sprint 1|0|2;S|A|Sprint 2|2|4;S|A|Sprint 3|4|6;S|A|Sprint 4|6|8;S|A|Sprint
      5|8|10;S|A|Sprint 6|10|12;R|A|2;R|A|4;R|A|6;R|A|8;R|A|10;R|A|12
    explanation: 'Waterfall plans every phase up front: 12 weeks and a single release
      at the end. The customer sees working software only at week 12.'
    narration: {fileID: 0}
  - highlightLine: 1
    action: add
    value: 0
    param: S|A|Sprint 1|0|2;S|A|Sprint 2|2|4;S|A|Sprint 3|4|6;S|A|Sprint 4|6|8;S|A|Sprint
      5|8|10;S|A|Sprint 6|10|12;R|A|2;R|A|4;R|A|6;R|A|8;R|A|10;R|A|12
    explanation: Agile plans six 2-week sprints. Every sprint ends with a release
      of working software, so the customer sees progress every 2 weeks.
    narration: {fileID: 0}
  - highlightLine: 2
    action: now
    value: 4
    param: 
    explanation: 'Week 4: Agile has already delivered 2 increments. Waterfall is
      still designing and starting to build, with nothing to show yet.'
    narration: {fileID: 0}
  - highlightLine: 2
    action: now
    value: 6
    param: 
    explanation: 'Week 6: Agile has delivered 3 increments. Waterfall is halfway
      through implementation.'
    narration: {fileID: 0}
  - highlightLine: 3
    action: add
    value: 0
    param: C|6;X|W|Implementation;X|W|Testing;X|W|Deployment;XR|W|12;S|W|Implementation
      (part 1)|4|6;S|W|Re-do Req.|6|7|rework;S|W|Re-do Design|7|8|rework;S|W|Implementation
      (resume)|8|13;S|W|Testing|13|15;S|W|Deployment|15|17;R|W|17;X|A|Sprint 4;S|A|Sprint
      4 + change|6|8|change
    explanation: 'Week 6: the customer changes a requirement! Waterfall must go back
      and redo Requirements and Design, so its release moves from week 12 to week
      17. Agile swaps the change in for a lower-priority story and keeps its dates.'
    narration: {fileID: 0}
  - highlightLine: 3
    action: now
    value: 8
    param: 
    explanation: 'Week 8: Agile ships Sprint 4 including the change. Waterfall has
      only just finished redoing its requirements and design'
    narration: {fileID: 0}
  - highlightLine: 3
    action: now
    value: 12
    param: 
    explanation: 'Week 12: Agile has delivered 6 working increments and the finished
      product. Waterfall is still implementing, and the customer has seen nothing.'
    narration: {fileID: 0}
  - highlightLine: 3
    action: now
    value: 17
    param: 
    explanation: 'Week 17: Waterfall finally releases, 5 weeks late. The customer
      sees working software only now.'
    narration: {fileID: 0}
  - highlightLine: 4
    action: none
    value: 0
    param: 
    explanation: 'Agile delivered early and absorbed the change. Trade-off: Agile
      needs an involved customer and flexible scope, while Waterfall suits fixed,
      well-understood requirements.'
    narration: {fileID: 0}
